  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: b3a9e1a4d1902c4d1b372ee0de810513, type: 3}
  m_Name: FrostStrangerOverExplain
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  RootNode:
    dialogueText: Well.<0.3>..</> How do I put this<0.3>...<0.000001>Well let me
      start with the tale of the lake above. Above here is a lake and on that lake
      are trees, and near the trees there is a lake. The lake is still but also moving,
      moving but still at the same time. What a paradox, did I mention the trees?
      So basically it was like always nighttime there, I found myself constantly
      staring at the moon. It seems all the other frogs see the moon the same, there's
      something enchanting about it really! There must be something there making
      the moon so enchanting. Oh yeah it was also RIDDLED with electricity and electricy
      and water don't mix, or I guess they mix a little too well, be careful there.
      But it was tool warm for my liking. That's why I'm out here! I like how cold
      it is, reminds me of home. Oh yeah and then there's the undergrowth oh my god
      they're so lazy! All of them. I mean I don't really blame them I they're kingdom's
      leader is a literral log. Like what is it going to do really? Like honestly?
      I don't know. Oh and finally before I forget there is there church of the heron.
      They're really crazy people man! They think that to put an end to the struggle
      over the castle is to summon and heron to eat all the frogs! They call it salvation,
      bunch of freaks bunch of freaks! Did you catch all that, I can go over it all
      again if you like?
    responses:
    - responseText: I'm not reading all that
      nextNode:
        dialogueText: Heh, yeah sorry I do that sometimes.<0.3> </>Listen to me though.<0.3>
          </>Please just help the castle, stop it from crumbling I miss how it used
          to be!
        responses:
        - responseText: Okay!
          nextNode:
            dialogueText: 
            responses: []
            onDialogue:
              m_PersistentCalls:
                m_Calls: []
          optionalNextDialogueTree: {fileID: 0}
        onDialogue:
          m_PersistentCalls:
            m_Calls: []
      optionalNextDialogueTree: {fileID: 0}
    - responseText: I read all that
      nextNode:
        dialogueText: <0.3>...</> No you didn't
        responses:
        - responseText: Yes I did
          nextNode:
            dialogueText: 
            responses: []
            onDialogue:
              m_PersistentCalls:
                m_Calls: []
          optionalNextDialogueTree: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 227c57cc3148977d5acd9d2afca559a3, type: 2}
        - responseText: You're right I lied
          nextNode:
            dialogueText: It's okay.<0.3> </>I do that sometimes.<0.3> </>Listen
              to me though.<0.3> </>Please just help the castle, stop it from crumbling
